## 7. REDESIGN THE VISUAL HIERARCHY

Do not treat the existing interface as a finished design with the wrong colours.

Review every page and ask:

- What is the main purpose of this page?
- What should the visitor notice first?
- Is the primary CTA obvious?
- Is the supporting information easy to scan?
- Are there too many competing visual elements?
- Are the sections too repetitive?
- Does the page have enough visual breathing room?
- Does the layout support the content?
- Does the design feel specific to ConsultAPP?

Improve weak layouts where necessary.

### Remove visual repetition

Avoid giving every section the same structure:

Heading → paragraph → three identical cards.

Use a more varied composition where it improves the experience.

Possible layouts include:

- Split editorial sections
- Asymmetric content and image layouts
- Horizontal feature arrangements
- Structured grids
- Full-width testimonial moments
- Alternating image and text sections
- Compact category collections
- Clear process timelines
- Distinct CTA sections

Use variety intentionally.

Do not add decorative elements simply to fill empty space.

### Whitespace

Use generous, consistent spacing.

Do not cram sections together.

Do not make the page excessively long through unnecessary padding.

Establish a coherent spacing system and use it consistently.

### Content width

Use a consistent maximum content width, generally around 1160–1240px depending on the existing layout.

Use responsive horizontal padding.

Prevent long text blocks from stretching across the entire viewport.

